{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit","id":1387025,"title":"Day Drinker Merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-09T11:41:45-07:00","id":1387025,"title":"Day Drinker Merit","content":"The merit says &quot;Sunlight halves your Health tracker (rounded up), but otherwise simply removes your vampiric abilities, including all Disciplines and Health benefits, and does no other damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> What all is included in &quot;your vampiric abilities&quot;? Obviously all disciplines weather through alchemy or affinity. I would assume healing. I would also assume blood surge. But what else? Your constant blush of life as a thin-blood? Your vampiric resilience if you have the merit? Your blood bonds if you have that merit? Your ability to ghoul? Your immortality as a vampire? Do you age? Can you die?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if I have missed something and where you guys would draw a hard line here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 05-09-2020, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T15:52:36-07:00","id":1387106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The merit says &quot;Sunlight halves your Health tracker (rounded up), but otherwise simply removes your vampiric abilities, including all Disciplines and Health benefits, and does no other damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> What all is included in &quot;your vampiric abilities&quot;? Obviously all disciplines weather through alchemy or affinity. I would assume healing. I would also assume blood surge. But what else? Your constant blush of life as a thin-blood? Your vampiric resilience if you have the merit? Your blood bonds if you have that merit? Your ability to ghoul? Your immortality as a vampire? Do you age? Can you die?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if I have missed something and where you guys would draw a hard line here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it as saying you're like a human in the daytime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T17:57:49-07:00","id":1387135,"title":"","content":"<br /> Here's a surprise... V5 is a little vague on this point, so I'm not sure there is a clear canon answer. Here's how I would handle it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The merit says &quot;Sunlight halves your Health tracker (rounded up), but otherwise simply removes your vampiric abilities, including all Disciplines and Health benefits, and does no other damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> What all is included in &quot;your vampiric abilities&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything a baseline, mundane human can't do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously all disciplines weather through alchemy or affinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I would allow any disciplines activated and set in motion as an independent effect to continue. So, if you Cloud Memory at 3am, then use Day Drinker starting at 6am, the memories don't flood back. You retain a Famulus, though temporarily lose all influence over them. Auspex shuts down. In Presence, Awe and Daunt cease functioning. Celerity and Potence are unavailable. Obfuscate shuts down.<br /> <br /> One edge case is Fortitude 1 (Resilience). Technically, the extra level of health could vanish in daylight, but since the Health tracker is already halved I would probably allow it to remain. I would not kill a pc over this. Plus, I suppose in theory some human somewhere might have lots of Health levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would assume healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, humans do heal, thank goodness. So, maybe normal human healing in a pinch? In general, avoid damage and heal damage at night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also assume blood surge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's off the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what else? Your constant blush of life as a thin-blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most humans have the ability to look like humans, so I would allow it. Please don't ask what to do if the TB has the clan flaw weakness for Nosferatu. I have no idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your vampiric resilience if you have the merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has &quot;vampiric&quot; in the name, so no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your blood bonds if you have that merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a self-sustaining effect, the bonds survive your stroll in sunshine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your ability to ghoul?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't feed someone new blood, at least no more effectively than a human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your immortality as a vampire? Do you age?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I would say you age during the day. Your hair and nails grow. Your pimples swell. Of course, as a vampire, everything returns to how it was at your embrace come sundown... so no noticeable aging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you die?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans can die. Helena, Augustus Giovanni, and Caine can all... in theory... die. If Cappadocius is to be believed, God can die, or at least be diablerized. So, yeah, you can die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit#post1387025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering if I have missed something and where you guys would draw a hard line here.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The biggie for me is the halving of Health levels. Picture it....<br /> <br /> Bob is a thinblood with the Daydrinker merit. He has six Health levels normally. He suffers four levels of Agg damage just before dawn and does not heal it. Later he is touched by the sun. His Health levels drop to three boxes, with four levels of damage. RAW, what happens? Does he just go poof? Enter torpor? Ordinarily, there might be dice involved at this point. Do you die from the halving of damage with no further damage?<br /> <br /> 2. You still have the Hunger. I assume you don't have fangs or the ability to lick feeding wounds to heal them. But, can you metabolize blood to feed? Normal humans can't.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T19:13:29-07:00","id":1387153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit?p=1387135#post1387135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bob is a thinblood with the Daydrinker merit. He has six Health levels normally. He suffers four levels of Agg damage just before dawn and does not heal it. Later he is touched by the sun. His Health levels drop to three boxes, with four levels of damage. RAW, what happens? Does he just go poof? Enter torpor? Ordinarily, there might be dice involved at this point. Do you die from the halving of damage with no further damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would personally say XXXXOO turns into XXO when halved. You're still at 2/3 of your maximum, the maximum is just lower. When he gets out of the sunlight again, he's back at XXXXOO.<br /> <br /> So no risk of dying just because the sun touched you\u2014but you're extremely fragile during the day, especially since you take damage like a mortal would (meaning mundane weapons do agg). In Bob's case, a single hit with any weapon at all, or two bare-handed punches, would torpor him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","user":"Draconis","date":". 05-09-2020, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T16:19:18-07:00","id":1387359,"title":"","content":"I'd probably view metabolizing consumed blood as one thing retained during the day, though feeding is obviously more difficult/dangerous and you can't use the blood to any real benefit other than reducing Hunger until night falls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T17:37:29-07:00","id":1387372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387025-day-drinker-merit?p=1387135#post1387135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. The biggie for me is the halving of Health levels. Picture it....<br /> <br /> Bob is a thinblood with the Daydrinker merit. He has six Health levels normally. He suffers four levels of Agg damage just before dawn and does not heal it. Later he is touched by the sun. His Health levels drop to three boxes, with four levels of damage. RAW, what happens? Does he just go poof? Enter torpor? Ordinarily, there might be dice involved at this point. Do you die from the halving of damage with no further damage?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If your health drops below your currently sustained damage levels as a result of this, you suffer the effects of Impairment or torpor (depending on type of damage) until you are clear of sunlight.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26131-leechesinmybreeches","name":"LeechesInMyBreeches","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}